USDT, also known as Tether, is a cryptocurrency called a stablecoin that is permanently pegged to the value of the United States Dollar (USD).
Unlike volatile cryptocurrencies like Bitcoin or Ethereum whose prices change drastically every minute, 1 USDT is designed to always be equal to $1 USD.
## How it Works in Simple Terms
Think of USDT as a digital dollar wrapper. For every single USDT token issued into the digital world, the parent company (Tether Limited) claims to hold exactly $1 USD in real-world bank reserves, short-term bonds, or cash equivalents to back it up.
Because it acts exactly like a dollar but moves over blockchain networks, it allows people all over the world to save, send, and trade in US dollars without needing a traditional American bank account.
