## Technical Networks: A Critical Warning
USDT does not have its own blockchain; instead, it "rides" on top of other networks. When you copy your wallet address to receive USDT, you must always make sure the network matches perfectly:

* TRC-20 (Tron Network): This is the most popular network used in Africa. It has very low fees (usually around $1 to $2 per transfer) and is incredibly fast.
* ERC-20 (Ethereum Network): This is much slower and has incredibly high gas fees (sometimes $5 to $20+ per transfer). Avoid this for small daily MoMo trades.

If someone sends you USDT via the TRC-20 network, but you give them an ERC-20 address, the funds will disappear into the blockchain completely, and no one can recover them.
